  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Malaria - Madagascar (01-Jul-2016-30-Jun-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Madagascar, Malaria, Population Services International (PSI HQ)This program has the following goals: By the end of 2017, to reduce malaria-related deaths to zero, and to reduce the test positivity rate to less than 5 percent in all districts. The objectives of this program are: Ensure that at least 80% of the targeted population adopts effective behaviours for prevention and control of malaria.  Ensure the correct management of at least 80% of malaria cases at different levels of the health system, including the private sector.  Protect at least 90 % of the population of targeted areas with effective malaria prevention measures, including insecticide-treated nets and indoor residual spraying.  Reach at least 80% of pregnant women in targeted areas with intermittent preventive treatment for malaria in accordance with the national policy of at least 3 doses.  Strengthen the institutional, technical and management capacity of the national malaria program at all levels, in order to consolidate the gains in malaria control.  Strengthen the M&amp;E system for malaria and ensure effective detection and management of 100% of outbreaks</narrative>
  </description>
